  "summary": "A dry screw vacuum pump has two parallel screw rotors that mesh without touching, synchronised by timing gears. Gas trapped in the threads is moved from the inlet (vacuum side) to the exhaust; a shorter pitch toward the exhaust compresses it internally. No oil or water is in the gas path, so the gas is not contaminated — ideal for chemical, pharmaceutical and semiconductor processes.",
